      "id": "zq35tal",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Importance of Agriculture in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "India has three distinct cropping seasons: Kharif (monsoon), Rabi (winter), and Zaid (summer).",
        "Rice is the predominant staple food crop, requiring high temperature (>25°C) and heavy rainfall (>100 cm).",
        "The Green Revolution introduced High Yielding Variety (HYV) seeds, expansion of irrigation, and modern fertilizers in the 1960s.",
        "Major cash crops including Cotton, Sugarcane, Jute, and Tea generate significant foreign exchange and industrial raw materials.",
        "Key government initiatives like PM-KISAN, PMFBY, and Soil Health Card aim to boost farm productivity and financial security."
      ],
      "id": "9s8749h"
    },
