      "id": "l75knt0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Government Initiatives"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Kharif crops (Rice, Maize, Cotton) depend on South-West Monsoon, whereas Rabi crops (Wheat, Mustard) rely on winter rainfall from Western Disturbances.",
        "Dr. M.S. Swaminathan is recognized as the Father of the Green Revolution in India.",
        "Operation Flood relates to Milk production (White Revolution), while Yellow Revolution focuses on Oilseeds.",
        "Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) fixes farmer premium at 2% for Kharif, 1.5% for Rabi, and 5% for commercial crops."
      ],
      "id": "1rtm567"
